| if text would break, and top navigation buttons are visible: same behaviour as described here: <custom data-type="smartlink" data-id="id-1">https://www.figma.com/design/92moLelAY8lh8mI0rhCGzy/laioutr-UI?node-id=8267-3&t=WGKlkG3l0TsCUryI-4</custom>   |  |
| the user can always decide to show or show not a scrollbar. |  |
| the navigation buttons are obligatory, but the user can decide if they should appear above the slider or under it |  |
| if all category nodes are visible on the screen (for example on large screens), the navigation elements are hidden |  |



## **Testing (stories):**

* Slider on light background - solid - naviagtion top - has scrollbar 
* slider on dark background - pale - navigation bottom - has scrollbar 
* slider on bright background - solid - navigation hidden - no scrollbar 
* slider on light background - pale - navigation bottom - has scrollbar - has action button

## **Technical details**:

_**organism/InpageNavigationCompactSlider**_

```
const InpageNavigationCompactSlider {
  colorMode: 'on-light' | 'on-dark' | 'on-bright';

  categoryNodesCompact : categoryNodeCompactProps[];

  header? : string;

  subline? : string;

  navigationPosition? : 'top' | 'bottom'

  hasScrollbar? : boolean;

  cta? : {
    text : string;
    link : string;
    variant : ButtonVariants
  }
}
```

‌

* if a CTA added the navigation position will be on bottom by default 
* please use `LuiCommonSwipper` for slider 
* do not use fixed css values for slides use slider options 
* hide navigation arrow if all the nodes are available
* components will be used `LuiText` ,`LuiButton`, `CategoryNodeBasic`,`LuiCommonSwipper` , `LuiSwiperNavigationCompact` , LuiSwipperScrollbar
